{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And these words.</b> And what is the love? <b>And these words</b> — for through this you come to recognize the Holy One, blessed be He, and to cleave to His ways (Sifrei)." "<b>Which I command you this day.</b> Let them not be in your eyes like an old דְּיוּטְגְּמָא that no one bothers with, but like a new one that everyone runs to read; דְּיוּטְגְּמָא — a royal command that arrives by letter (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "דיוטגמא is from Greek διάταγμα, 'decree/edict.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:09.079717270Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}